.TH ORCA 1 "2026-06-18" "Orca 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
orca \- full-featured, security-focused Linux file manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B orca-gui
.RI [ OPTION ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Orca
is a Wayland-first Linux file manager written in Rust with GTK4.
It provides a dual-pane browser, integrated encrypted vaults, a sandboxed
Lua plugin API, and extensive keyboard-driven navigation.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version string and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Controls log verbosity.
Default:
.BR info .
Accepted values (least to most verbose):
.BR error ,
.BR warn ,
.BR info ,
.BR debug ,
.BR trace .
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base directory for the user configuration file
.RB ( config.toml ).
Default:
.IR ~/.config .
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Base directory for data files (vaults, themes, plugins).
Default:
.IR ~/.local/share .
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Base directory for thumbnail cache.
Default:
.IR ~/.cache .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/orca/config.toml
User configuration. Written with defaults on first run.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/orca/plugins/
User Lua plugins.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/orca/themes/
User CSS themes.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/orca/vaults/
Default vault storage directory.
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/orca/thumbnails/
Thumbnail cache (XDG thumbnail spec).
.SH DEFAULT KEYBINDINGS
.TS
tab(|) allbox;
lb lb
l l.
Action|Keybind
New tab|Ctrl+T
Close tab|Ctrl+W
Toggle hidden files|Ctrl+H
Toggle terminal panel|F4
Toggle preview panel|F7
Toggle dual pane|F3
Inline rename|F2
Back|Alt+Left
Forward|Alt+Right
Up|Alt+Up
Search|Ctrl+F
Edit path|Ctrl+L
List view|Ctrl+1
Icon view|Ctrl+2
Detail view|Ctrl+3
.TE
.PP
All keybinds are rebindable in Settings → Keyboard Shortcuts.
.SH PLUGIN API
Plugins are Lua 5.4 scripts with access to the
.B orca.*
namespace. They run in a sandbox that blocks
.BR io ,
.BR os ,
.BR package ,
and
.BR debug .
See
.I /usr/share/doc/orca/plugins.md
for the full API reference.
